From f9bfce56b35a38ce17ae26bace9e33997d23b4d8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TuNV <tunguyenvanbn94@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 15:13:35 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] [icwmp tr098] P5d+P5e: Layer3Forwarding and the hidden root
 diagnostics; phase 5 complete

Layer3Forwarding (12 parameters), from functions/tr098/layer3_forwarding.
Static routes are the anonymous network "route" sections; the default WAN
is wan.@entry[].default_gw.

The vendor paths are kept: Enable, ForwardNumberOfEntries and
DefaultConnectionService sit on Layer3Forwarding.Forwarding. itself, next
to its instances.  The engine gave a multi-instance object's leaves to its
instances only, so DMOBJ grows a last member, container_leaf, browsed on
the container node before the instances (dmtr098.c dm_browse), merged by
the registry.  Existing positional initializers leave it NULL.

The two WAN-path setters are ported as busybox 1.33.1 really runs them
(shell/ash.c, coreutils/test.c): inside [[ ]] ash passes && and || to test
as words, so "[[ ! $node =~ ^WAN... || ! is_integer $index ]]" leaves an
operand over and exits 2 for every value -- it never rejects, nor does the
"-le 1" line after it.  What decides is the prefix, awk -F. field NF-2 /
NF-1, ash arithmetic for index-1, and an entry with that id and a matching
conn_type.  Forwarding.{i}.Interface goes through UCI package "hniwan",
which exists nowhere in the SDK: kept literally.

SelfTestDiagnostics and WiFi.NeighboringWiFiDiagnostic (3 parameters) are
hidden on the product: the root entry is a "case" on the requested path
and answers them only when asked by name.  DMOBJ.addressed_only makes the
engine skip such an object unless in_param lies under it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
